  "imageName": "textformat.size",
  "intro": "Adjectives must match their nouns in case. In accusative, the key rule is: ANIMATE MASCULINE adjectives look like GENITIVE (-ого/-его), while everything else looks like NOMINATIVE. So 'new book' → 'новую книгу' (fem acc = -ую), but 'new student' → 'нового студента' (animate masc = -ого). Feminine and neuter have their own distinct endings.",
  "rules": [
    "Adjective accusative depends on whether the noun is animate or inanimate (masculine only).",
    "Feminine adjective accusative is always -ую/-юю, regardless of animacy.",
    "Neuter adjective accusative always matches nominative (-ое/-ее).",
    "Plural animate adjectives use genitive form (-ых/-их), inanimate use nominative (-ые/-ие)."
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Я читаю интересную книгу. (I'm reading an interesting book.), fem: -ая → -ую",
    "Я вижу старого друга. (I see an old friend.), animate masc: -ый → -ого",
    "Он купил новый телефон. (He bought a new phone.), inanimate masc: same as nom",
    "Она любит синее море. (She loves the blue sea.), neuter: same as nom"
  ],
